---
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<section class="module-deck" aria-label="Explore Instar">
  <article class="portal-card portal-card--start">
    <header><h2>START</h2><span aria-hidden="true">▣</span></header>
    <div class="portal-card-body">
      <p class="kicker">instar / new user</p>
      <h3>Open a real native window.</h3>
      <div class="mini-terminal"><code>instar run counter.wasm</code></div>
      <p>Install the host, build the included counter, and run it through the real runtime.</p>
      <ul class="tiny-links">
        <li><a href="/docs/getting-started/install">Install Instar</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/getting-started/first-run">First run</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <footer>macOS / Linux / Windows</footer>
  </article>

  <article class="portal-card portal-card--build">
    <header><h2>BUILD</h2><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></header>
    <div class="portal-card-body">
      <p class="kicker">guest / component</p>
      <div class="mini-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Guest sends a snapshot to the host">
        <span>GUEST</span><b>→</b><span>SNAPSHOT</span><b>→</b><span>HOST</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Describe meaning, not pixels.</h3>
      <p>The component commits retained UI snapshots and waits for semantic events.</p>
      <ul class="tiny-links">
        <li><a href="/docs/getting-started/build-a-guest">Build a guest</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/reference/ui-vocabulary">UI vocabulary</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <footer>Rust / wasm32-wasip2 / WIT</footer>
  </article>

  <article class="portal-card portal-card--learn">
    <header><h2>RUNTIME</h2><span aria-hidden="true">✦</span></header>
    <div class="portal-card-body">
      <p class="kicker">host / authority</p>
      <div class="owner-map" role="img" aria-label="Your app and Wasm guest run over the Instar native host">
        <span>YOUR APP</span><span>WASM GUEST</span><b>INSTAR NATIVE HOST</b>
      </div>
      <h3>The host keeps authority.</h3>
      <p>A guest can fail without taking the native surface or accessibility tree with it.</p>
      <ul class="tiny-links">
        <li><a href="/docs/concepts/runtime-model">Runtime model</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/concepts/host-owned-ui">Host-owned UI</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <footer>zero idle polling / bounded queues</footer>
  </article>

  <article class="portal-card portal-card--download">
    <header><h2>DOWNLOAD</h2><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></header>
    <div class="portal-card-body">
      <p class="kicker">developer preview / source</p>
      <h3>Install the native host.</h3>
      <div class="command-box">
        <code>{site.installCommand}</code>
        <button class="button-orange" type="button" data-copy={site.installCommand}>COPY</button>
      </div>
      <p>No tagged binary exists yet; the installer points to the honest source-build path.</p>
      <ul class="tiny-links">
        <li><a href="/downloads">All downloads</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/development/build-from-source">Build from source</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <footer>0.0.2 / no stability promise</footer>
  </article>
</section>
